+Reject a ``VTIMEZONE`` whose ``RRULE`` produces more than :data:`~icalendar.config.MAX_TIMEZONE_TRANSITIONS_PER_YEAR` transitions within a year, ``100`` by default. Timezones created from a ``VTIMEZONE`` expand its ``RRULE`` from ``DTSTART``, so a calendar with an ``RRULE`` such as ``FREQ=SECONDLY`` in a ``VTIMEZONE`` could exhaust memory and CPU when it was parsed or when a date in that timezone was used. I used AI to assist me with this change. @shamsManna
